# Dependency hygiene

REQ-01: Authorized full verification uses the maintainer-selected Toolbox path.
REQ-02: Reviewed dependency licenses are explicitly permitted without relicensing Ox.
REQ-03: Temporarily ignore only the two adopted unmaintained advisory IDs; other advisories remain enforced.
REQ-04: Remove resolvable duplicate versions without deleting required dependencies or silently hiding incompatible constraints.

- AC-01 → REQ-01: The operational rule names the exact executable and retains explicit execution authorization.
- AC-02 → REQ-02: License inventory matches source identities and the native license check accepts the selected graph.
- AC-03 → REQ-03: Two exact IDs are ignored by native policy while unknown/security findings remain failures.
- AC-04 → REQ-04: Duplicate reduction is measured; any irreducible constraints have an explicit maintainer disposition and no false claim of elimination.
